{
    "chapter_num": 9,
    "verses_count": 50,
    "paragraphs_list": [
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 1,
                    "num_str": "1",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And he said to them, “Truly, I say to you, there are some standing here who will not taste death before they see that the kingdom of God has come with power.”"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "The Transfiguration"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 2,
                    "num_str": "2",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And after six days Jesus took with him Peter and James and John, and led them up a high mountain apart by themselves; and he was transfigured before them, "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 3,
                    "num_str": "3",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "and his garments became glistening, intensely white, as no fuller on earth could bleach them. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 4,
                    "num_str": "4",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And there appeared to them Eli′jah with Moses; and they were talking to Jesus. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 5,
                    "num_str": "5",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And Peter said to Jesus, “Master,"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Or Rabbi"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " it is well that we are here; let us make three booths, one for you and one for Moses and one for Eli′jah.” "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 6,
                    "num_str": "6",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "For he did not know what to say, for they were exceedingly afraid. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 7,
                    "num_str": "7",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And a cloud overshadowed them, and a voice came out of the cloud, “This is my beloved Son;"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Or my Son, my (or the) Beloved"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " listen to him.” "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 8,
                    "num_str": "8",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And suddenly looking around they no longer saw any one with them but Jesus only."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "The Coming of Elijah"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 9,
                    "num_str": "9",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And as they were coming down the mountain, he charged them to tell no one what they had seen, until the Son of man should have risen from the dead. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 10,
                    "num_str": "10",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "So they kept the matter to themselves, questioning what the rising from the dead meant. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 11,
                    "num_str": "11",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And they asked him, “Why do the scribes say that first Eli′jah must come?” "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 12,
                    "num_str": "12",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And he said to them, “Eli′jah does come first to restore all things; and how is it written of the Son of man, that he should suffer many things and be treated with contempt? "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 13,
                    "num_str": "13",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "But I tell you that Eli′jah has come, and they did to him whatever they pleased, as it is written of him.”"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "The Healing of a Boy with a Spirit"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 14,
                    "num_str": "14",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And when they came to the disciples, they saw a great crowd about them, and scribes arguing with them. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 15,
                    "num_str": "15",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And immediately all the crowd, when they saw him, were greatly amazed, and ran up to him and greeted him. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 16,
                    "num_str": "16",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And he asked them, “What are you discussing with them?” "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 17,
                    "num_str": "17",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And one of the crowd answered him, “Teacher, I brought my son to you, for he has a dumb spirit; "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 18,
                    "num_str": "18",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "and wherever it seizes him, it dashes him down; and he foams and grinds his teeth and becomes rigid; and I asked your disciples to cast it out, and they were not able.” "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 19,
                    "num_str": "19",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And he answered them, “O faithless generation, how long am I to be with you? How long am I to bear with you? Bring him to me.” "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 20,
                    "num_str": "20",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And they brought the boy to him; and when the spirit saw him, immediately it convulsed the boy, and he fell on the ground and rolled about, foaming at the mouth. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 21,
                    "num_str": "21",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And Jesus"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Greek he"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " asked his father, “How long has he had this?” And he said, “From childhood. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 22,
                    "num_str": "22",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And it has often cast him into the fire and into the water, to destroy him; but if you can do anything, have pity on us and help us.” "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 23,
                    "num_str": "23",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And Jesus said to him, “If you can! All things are possible to him who believes.” "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 24,
                    "num_str": "24",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Immediately the father of the child cried out"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Other ancient authorities add with tears"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " and said, “I believe; help my unbelief!” "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 25,
                    "num_str": "25",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And when Jesus saw that a crowd came running together, he rebuked the unclean spirit, saying to it, “You dumb and deaf spirit, I command you, come out of him, and never enter him again.” "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 26,
                    "num_str": "26",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And after crying out and convulsing him terribly, it came out, and the boy was like a corpse; so that most of them said, “He is dead.” "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 27,
                    "num_str": "27",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "But Jesus took him by the hand and lifted him up, and he arose. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 28,
                    "num_str": "28",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And when he had entered the house, his disciples asked him privately, “Why could we not cast it out?” "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 29,
                    "num_str": "29",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And he said to them, “This kind cannot be driven out by anything but prayer.”"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Other ancient authorities add and fasting"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "Jesus Again Foretells His Death and Resurrection"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 30,
                    "num_str": "30",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "They went on from there and passed through Galilee. And he would not have any one know it; "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 31,
                    "num_str": "31",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "for he was teaching his disciples, saying to them, “The Son of man will be delivered into the hands of men, and they will kill him; and when he is killed, after three days he will rise.” "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 32,
                    "num_str": "32",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "But they did not understand the saying, and they were afraid to ask him."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "Who Is the Greatest?"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 33,
                    "num_str": "33",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And they came to Caper′na-um; and when he was in the house he asked them, “What were you discussing on the way?” "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 34,
                    "num_str": "34",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "But they were silent; for on the way they had discussed with one another who was the greatest. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 35,
                    "num_str": "35",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And he sat down and called the twelve; and he said to them, “If any one would be first, he must be last of all and servant of all.” "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 36,
                    "num_str": "36",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And he took a child, and put him in the midst of them; and taking him in his arms, he said to them, "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 37,
                    "num_str": "37",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "“Whoever receives one such child in my name receives me; and whoever receives me, receives not me but him who sent me.”"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "Another Exorcist"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 38,
                    "num_str": "38",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "John said to him, “Teacher, we saw a man casting out demons in your name,"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Other ancient authorities add who does not follow us"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " and we forbade him, because he was not following us.” "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 39,
                    "num_str": "39",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "But Jesus said, “Do not forbid him; for no one who does a mighty work in my name will be able soon after to speak evil of me. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 40,
                    "num_str": "40",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "For he that is not against us is for us. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 41,
                    "num_str": "41",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "For truly, I say to you, whoever gives you a cup of water to drink because you bear the name of Christ, will by no means lose his reward."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "Temptations to Sin"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 42,
                    "num_str": "42",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "“Whoever causes one of these little ones who believe in me to sin,"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Greek stumble"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " it would be better for him if a great millstone were hung round his neck and he were thrown into the sea. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 43,
                    "num_str": "43",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And if your hand causes you to sin,"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Greek stumble"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " cut it off; it is better for you to enter life maimed than with two hands to go to hell,"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Greek Gehenna"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " to the unquenchable fire."
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Verses 44 and 46 (which are identical with verse 48) are omitted by the best ancient authorities"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 45,
                    "num_str": "45",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And if your foot causes you to sin,"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Greek stumble"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " cut it off; it is better for you to enter life lame than with two feet to be thrown into hell."
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Greek GehennaVerses 44 and 46 (which are identical with verse 48) are omitted by the best ancient authorities"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 47,
                    "num_str": "47",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And if your eye causes you to sin,"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Greek stumble"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " pluck it out; it is better for you to enter the kingdom of God with one eye than with two eyes to be thrown into hell,"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Greek Gehenna"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 48,
                    "num_str": "48",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "where their worm does not die, and the fire is not quenched. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 49,
                    "num_str": "49",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "For every one will be salted with fire."
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Other ancient authorities add and every sacrifice will be salted with salt"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 50,
                    "num_str": "50",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Salt is good; but if the salt has lost its saltness, how will you season it? Have salt in yourselves, and be at peace with one another.”"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        }
    ]
}